  "worked_solution": "Taking the square root of both sides of the inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\ge 5 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{5} \\\\ |x| & \\ge \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the definition of absolute value, we must have\n\n$$\nx\\le -\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{or}\\,x\\ge \\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\sqrt{5}]\\cup [\\sqrt{5},\\infty ).$",
